<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Learning to Balance – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Learning to Balance</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How to Balance Social and School Activities</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write reflective essays on personal experiences. Interactive: Write a group text on various topics, collaboratively, to be shared in a digital format.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a reflective essay on the experience of balancing school and personal life (e.g., "In my essay, I'll describe how to manage my schoolwork alongside personal activities like sports and volunteering.")
Can collaboratively write a digital text about learning to relax or maintaining school-life balance (e.g., "Take breaks during study sessions and make time for hobbies to relax and recharge.")
Can exchange drafts and provide feedback to improve the group's digital text (e.g., "Suggest ways to make the blog post more engaging for readers.")</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 57%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 10%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher initiates a "Quick Write & Share" activity. Students are asked to think about their busiest week recently and quickly jot down 2-3 school *activities* and 2-3 social *hobbies* or *activities* they engaged in. Then, they write one sentence describing how they *felt* about their *balance* that week, using adjectives like *overwhelming*, *calm*, *busy*, or *productive*. (e.g., "Last week was *overwhelming* because I had too many *activities* and no *downtime*.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models reflecting on personal balance by writing a sentence on the board: "I *have been trying* to *manage* my *workload* for weeks, but it *might* be difficult to *prioritize* everything without a clear *schedule*." The teacher highlights the use of Present Perfect Continuous and a modal for possibility, and target vocabulary.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of key terms and grammar points.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'I have been studying,' does it mean I finished or I'm still doing it, or it's an ongoing effort?" (Ongoing effort.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'balance' about having only one type of activity, or a mix of different *activities*?" (A mix.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Pronunciation check): "Listen to 'activities' /ækˈtɪvɪtɪz/ and 'relieve' /rɪˈliːv/. What's the difference in the main vowel sound?" (Short /ɪ/ vs. long /iː/). The teacher might dictate words for students to write down to check spelling and sound awareness.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Learning to Balance".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short reflective essay excerpt (approx. 150 words) from a high school student's blog titled "My Journey to a Balanced Life: School, Friends, and Me" (narrative excerpt, informal register, digital format connection). The text details the student's personal experience and strategies for managing *stress* and finding *flexibility* in their *schedule*.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Writing reflective essays on personal experiences and identifying key strategies for *balance*.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the blog post excerpt silently.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What is the main message or challenge the author is trying to convey about *learning to balance*?" (Students write their answer).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False statements:</b> Students write T or F for statements based on the text (e.g., "The author *has been struggling* to find *downtime* recently." "If the author *had* more *flexibility*, they *would* spend more time volunteering.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Identify & Underline:</b> Students identify and underline all instances of Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, and Modals for possibility (should, might, could) related to giving *suggestions* or expressing *opinions* within the text. They also highlight 5 new vocabulary words (e.g., *mindfulness*, *wellbeing*, *procrastination*, *allocate*, *restorative*).</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice constructing grammatically correct sentences using Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, and Modals for possibility, integrating target vocabulary words related to *balance*, *stress*, *relaxation*, and *time management* in written form.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Sentence Completion (Controlled Practice):</b> Students complete 5-7 sentences by filling in the blanks with the correct form of the verb (Present Perfect Continuous) or choosing the appropriate modal/conditional. Example: "I _______ (try) to improve my *routine* by *scheduling* breaks, but it _______ (be) hard to avoid *procrastination*." (Answer: *have been trying*, *might be*). "If I ______ (have) a *balanced* *schedule*, I ______ (feel) less *stress*." (Answer: *had*, *would feel*).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Sentence Expansion (Semi-Controlled Practice):</b> The teacher provides simple sentences or prompts. Students rewrite and expand them, incorporating at least one target grammar structure (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, or a Modal of possibility) and 2-3 target vocabulary words. Example prompt: "Manage stress. Get more sleep." Student writes: "I *have been trying* to *manage stress* by setting *boundaries* for my *social life*, and if I *got* more sleep, I *would feel* more *restorative*."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Collaborative Suggestion Writing:</b> In pairs, students select three different aspects of school-life balance (e.g., *workload*, *downtime*, *social life*) and write one suggestion for each, using a different modal verb (*should*, *might*, *could*) for each suggestion. They must also incorporate 1-2 new vocabulary words in each suggestion. Example: "You *should* *prioritize* your *activities* to reduce *overwhelming* feelings." (This promotes collaborative writing and giving suggestions.)</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Learning to Balance".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> This stage involves two distinct writing tasks, reinforcing both productive and interactive writing outcomes.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Part 1: Reflective Essay (Individual Writing):</b> Students will write a short reflective essay (150-200 words) on their personal experiences of *balancing* school and personal life. The essay should describe challenges, ongoing efforts, and hypothetical improvements. Students must integrate:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one instance of Present Perfect Continuous (e.g., "I *have been studying* late...").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one instance of the Second Conditional (e.g., "If I *had* more *downtime*, I *would join* a club...").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one Modal for possibility to suggest a personal strategy (e.g., "I *might need* to *organize* my *schedule* better...").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A minimum of 5 specified vocabulary words (e.g., *flexibility*, *wellbeing*, *prioritize*, *stress*, *relaxation*).</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Part 2: Collaborative Digital Text (Group Writing):</b> In groups of 3-4, students will collaboratively write a short digital text (e.g., a blog post, social media guide, or infographic content, 100-150 words) titled "Our Top Tips for a Balanced Life." This text should offer *suggestions* for *learning to relax* or maintaining school-life *balance*. Groups must explicitly *give suggestions* using modals (*should*, *could*, *might*) and *express opinions* on balance, integrating relevant vocabulary. (Sociolinguistic: Encouraging inclusive communication and sharing cultural perspectives on stress management strategies).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme/Scenario:</b> These tasks directly address "How to Balance Social and School Activities" by requiring students to reflect on and articulate their own experiences and provide practical advice for "Learning to Balance."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in written expression, accurate application of target grammar and vocabulary, and effective collaborative interaction for the digital text.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer feedback on individual essays and teacher observation of group collaboration and final digital text.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Peer Feedback:</b> Students exchange their reflective essays (Part 1) with a partner. Using a provided checklist, they offer constructive feedback focused on clarity, use of target grammar/vocabulary, and suggestions to make the essay more engaging.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Group Review:</b> Each group posts their "Our Top Tips for a Balanced Life" digital text (Part 2) on a shared digital platform (e.g., Google Docs, class blog). The teacher reviews these for completion and quality.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher & Peer):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and cohesion of written ideas in both essay and group text.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate and appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., *mindfulness*, *wellbeing*, *procrastination*, *allocate*, *restorative*).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct application of Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, and Modals for possibility.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective *giving of suggestions* and *expressing opinions* (for group text).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaborative engagement and inclusive communication within groups.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following prompts in writing:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new thing you learned about your own *time management* or *stress relief* strategies while writing today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one specific aspect of your writing (grammar, vocabulary, organization) you want to improve in the next writing task?"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did writing a reflective essay and a collaborative digital text help you better understand the nuances of *balancing* *social life* and *school activities*?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Based on your self-assessment and peer feedback, what is one actionable step you *might take* to enhance your academic writing skills?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> "Did students demonstrate sufficient mastery of the target grammar structures (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, Modals for possibility) and vocabulary in their individual reflective essays and collaborative digital texts? Were the writing prompts challenging enough for their B1.3 level? What common errors were observed in grammar or vocabulary usage, and how can these be addressed? Were the peer feedback and self-assessment activities effective in promoting learning? What adjustments to scaffolding or instruction are needed for future writing lessons to further develop their ability to write complex, coherent texts?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> "In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), we will take our collaboratively written digital texts and compile them into a class 'Balance Handbook.' Students will then mediate by summarizing key strategies from other groups, and we will integrate all learned concepts into a final project about promoting *wellbeing* and *balanced routines* in our school community."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>